{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786509618,"nonce":"PqMr4E3O3LHwia0ZPJMxTdmIGuY=","target":"fc383987df522b6d7eea071c2ff6385d5ed2bd9852ecbafc278030300beeb8bb","message":"**What is wrong.** The chart is real: `deploy/helm/oto/` is 13 templates, 1,131 lines of them, over a 570-line `values.yaml`. **No part of it is executed by anything.** The strings `helm lint`, `helm template`, `helm package` and `helm push` appear in no `.yml`, `.yaml`, `.md`, `.go`, `.sh` or `justfile` in the repository. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` has eight jobs and none of them installs Helm; `just ci` (`justfile:311`) chains nine recipes and none of them touches `deploy/`. The chart's correctness is asserted by review only.\n\n**The demonstration.** `templates/_helpers.tpl:163-192` defines `oto.validateValues`: **eight `fail` calls** (`:165`, `:168`, `:171`, `:174`, `:179`, `:183`, `:186`, `:189`) that exist specifically to stop a bad install with a sentence instead of a CrashLoopBackOff — a missing `databaseUrl`, a comma in the DSN, `slack.mode: http` with no signing secret, an out-of-range `config.env`, a connection split that starves the general pool, and three bootstrap preconditions. The pool-exhaustion guard at `:176-180` does integer arithmetic in Go templates. A typo in any of those expressions — a mis-nested `{{- if -}}`, an `.Values` path that no longer exists after a values rename, a guard inverted so it fires on the happy path — is discovered by the first operator to run `helm install`, because nothing here has ever been rendered outside a human's head. The same is true of every `{{ include }}` in the other twelve templates.\n\n**Why it matters.** oto's whole go-to-market is the install (SPEC R7 at `docs/design/SPEC.md:40`, acceptance criterion 31 at `:3811`, ADR 0001, ADR 0014, ADR 0015 — all four argue the one-`helm install` story as a product asset). Every other contract in this repository has a gate: G1 through G4 in `ci.yml`, the vocabulary gate at `ci.yml:176`, the reachability gate at `:194`. The chart — the single artifact a customer touches first — is the only one with none.\n\nThree separate things are missing, and only the first is a gate:\n\n1. **Render the chart in CI.** A `helm` job that runs `helm lint deploy/helm/oto` and then `helm template` at least three ways: defaults plus `secrets.databaseUrl` (the happy path must render), `--set ingress.enabled=true --set api.autoscaling.enabled=true --set bootstrap.enabled=true,bootstrap.orgSlug=acme,bootstrap.email=a@b.c` (so `ingress.yaml`, `hpa.yaml`, `pdb.yaml` and `job-bootstrap.yaml` are rendered at all — at the defaults `ingress.enabled` is `false` (`values.yaml:300`), `autoscaling.enabled` is `false` (`:249`) and `bootstrap.enabled` is `false` (`:174`), so three templates are invisible to any single render), and `--set existingSecret=oto-secrets` (which must render **no** Secret, per `_helpers.tpl:73-74`). Each of the eight `fail` guards should be asserted to fire on its own bad input; a guard that no longer fires is exactly the reachability defect class `tools/lintreach` exists for, one layer out. Per `README.md:76-79` the gate must land in **both** `ci.yml` and the `just ci` list, or a contributor's green stops meaning anything.\n\n2. **The `appVersion` coupling.** `values.yaml:47` leaves `image.tag` empty and `_helpers.tpl:63-66` falls back to `.Chart.AppVersion`, which `Chart.yaml:14` sets to `\"0.1.0\"`. That design is right — it is not a floating `latest`, and `values.yaml:44-46` says why in the chart's own voice. What is missing is that nothing couples `appVersion` to anything that exists: `git tag` lists zero tags, so the default install requests an image tag no release ever produced, and on the day releases start nothing fails when `appVersion` and the newest tag diverge. The `helm` job should assert that the rendered image reference matches the repository's newest release tag (or, before the first release, that `values.yaml:39-42`'s ⚠️ *\"NO IMAGE IS PUBLISHED YET\"* is still true — a disclaimer nothing checks is the defect class this repo keeps rediscovering). `Chart.version` (`:9`) is likewise hand-maintained with no check that a templates change bumped it.\n\n3. **Publish the chart.** Helm 3 speaks OCI, so `helm package` + `helm push … oci://ghcr.io/\u003cowner\u003e/charts` needs the same `packages: write` and the same `GITHUB_TOKEN` as the image. Today `oci://` appears in no file in the tree and no document gives a `helm repo add` line, so the only install path in existence is *clone the repository and point Helm at a local directory*. That is not the install acceptance criterion 31 describes.\n\nTo be clear about what is **not** wrong, because it would be easy to assume: `image.pullPolicy` is set (`values.yaml:48`), `imagePullSecrets` is wired (`:51`), and requests and limits are set for all four workloads (`:147-152`, `:186-191`, `:208-213`, `:270-275`). The values file is in good shape. This ticket is CI plumbing plus one version-coupling check, not a chart rewrite.\n\n**Where.** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (no `helm` job), `justfile:311` (the `ci` list), `deploy/helm/oto/templates/_helpers.tpl:63-66` and `:163-192`, `deploy/helm/oto/Chart.yaml:9` and `:14`, `deploy/helm/oto/values.yaml:39-47`.\n\n**Coupled to the `release` ticket, which lands first.** A chart cannot be published referring to an image that does not exist: the OCI chart push and the image push want the same tag, the same `packages: write` grant and the same `GITHUB_TOKEN`, and the `appVersion` check in (2) has nothing to compare against until a release tag exists. Item (1) — `helm lint` and `helm template` in CI — is independent and can land immediately; items (2) and (3) follow the release workflow.\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** A `helm` job in `ci.yml`, mirrored into `just ci`, runs `helm lint` and renders the chart in the four value combinations above; a deliberately planted template typo and a deliberately broken guard both fail that job (the standard `docs/ORCHESTRATION.md:102-103` records for G1–G4); the rendered image tag is checked against the newest release tag; and `helm install oto oci://ghcr.io/\u003cowner\u003e/charts/oto --version \u003cchart version\u003e --set secrets.databaseUrl=…` installs a working release without the repository being cloned.","files":null}]}